 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? That's common problem. To fix it, draw two eyes on separate sheets of paper first, without looking at the face. It' worth a try. Pick the eyes that look about right, even if the eyes are in different places. Then try drawing them on the face with that in mind. Draw the nose before the face, but make it small. Then add the eyes and mouth. Good. And don't worry too much about getting it right. Drawing is a lot about learning from your mistakes.",
